WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.110
Rhiannon: Mental health services are
free on the NHS, but in some cases a

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.490
GP referral is needed to access them.

00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:11.209
However, there are some mental
health services that allow

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:12.839
people to refer themselves.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:18.129
At school or college, mental health
care can be arranged for individuals

00:00:18.209 --> 00:00:23.980
through services such as CYPMHS
which we have discussed previously.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.939
Leah: Some mental health problems
can be managed without the need of

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.680
approaching a GP and there are a
variety of materials available and

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:34.949
local organisations offering help.

00:00:35.669 --> 00:00:40.168
Rhiannon: A GP will assess an individual’s
circumstances and offer appropriate

00:00:40.168 --> 00:00:45.318
advice or treatment and can refer an
individual on to a psychological therapy

00:00:45.318 --> 00:00:50.238
service or a specialist mental health
service for further advice or treatment.

00:00:50.998 --> 00:00:55.368
These services may be provided
by a GP surgery, a large local

00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:59.118
health centre, a specialist mental
health clinic or a hospital.

00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:06.848
Treatment may be provided on a one-to-one
basis or in a group with others with

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:11.588
similar difficulties, and therapy
can also sometimes involve families.

00:01:16.068 --> 00:01:19.898
Leah: An Individual has the legal right
to choose which provider and clinical

00:01:19.898 --> 00:01:24.498
team they are referred to by their GP for
their first outpatient appointment and in

00:01:24.498 --> 00:01:28.868
most cases, have the right to choose which
mental health service provider to go to.

00:01:29.508 --> 00:01:33.518
Rhiannon: However, this right is not
there for urgent or emergency treatment,

00:01:33.798 --> 00:01:37.638
where treatment and care is already
being received, if the condition isn’t

00:01:37.638 --> 00:01:41.928
covered by that team, or the child
or young person is being detained.

00:01:42.918 --> 00:01:46.968
some services available on the NHS
are for Psychological Therapies

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:51.328
anxiety and depression, eating
disorders, mental health services.

00:01:51.338 --> 00:01:53.798
for alcohol addiction,
and for drug misuse.

00:01:56.508 --> 00:02:01.378
Once a mental health service provider
has been decided on an appointment can

00:02:01.378 --> 00:02:05.958
be booked through the NHS e-Referral
Service or via a doctor’s surgery.

00:02:06.908 --> 00:02:11.378
Early access to mental health services
regardless of age, ethnicity, gender

00:02:11.448 --> 00:02:14.848
or social status may reduce the
risk of problems becoming worse.

